                <h2>Pre-Launch Creative Preparation Checklist</h2>
<p>Before launching ads, ensure your creative pool covers core scenarios:</p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] <strong>Extract core product selling points</strong>: Convert 3-5 differentiated points from your detail page into 15-second visual messages</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Basic product videos</strong>: Complete at least 3 pure product showcase videos (multiple angles, feature demos, close-ups)</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Usage scenario videos</strong>: Cover 2-3 typical user scenarios like "office afternoon tea" or "outdoor activities"</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Comparison content</strong>: Create 1-2 videos comparing with similar products on the market</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>UGC-style content</strong>: Shoot 2-3 authentic-feeling unboxing or first-impression videos</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Captions and copy</strong>: Prepare 3 different CTA copy styles for each video</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Multiple aspect ratios</strong>: 16:9, 9:16, and 1:1 versions (at least 2 each)</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Localization</strong>: Complete subtitles and voiceover for target markets</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Pitfall Alert</strong>: Many teams start with only 1-2 creatives during cold start, leading to insufficient testing dimensions. Aim for 8-10 creatives per product before launching.</p>
</blockquote>
<h2>Phased Testing Execution Checklist</h2>
<h3>Phase 1: Days 1-7, Rapid Scaling Test</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] <strong>Set test budget</strong>: Initial budget of ¥100-200 per creative for quick data acquisition</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Enable automatic allocation</strong>: Let TikTok's system find optimal audiences faster</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Track initial CTR</strong>: Monitor click rates from first 1,000 impressions to judge appeal</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Flag high performers</strong>: Creatives with 20%+ above category average CTR move to next phase</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Pause low performers</strong>: Suspend creatives with below 15% video completion rate</li>
</ul>
<h3>Phase 2: Days 8-21, Creative Scaling Verification</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] <strong>Combination testing</strong>: Mix high performers with new creatives to test synergy</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Audience split testing</strong>: Test creative performance across age, interest, and behavior segments</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Bid strategy adjustment</strong>: Increase bids on high performers to accelerate data collection</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Landing page alignment check</strong>: Ensure creative and detail page messaging match</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Record ROI baseline</strong>: Calculate cost per conversion compared to category average CAC</li>
</ul>
<h3>Phase 3: Days 22-30, Creative Pool Optimization</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] <strong>Build creative scoring system</strong>: Score based on CTR, CVR, completion rate, and ROI</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Eliminate bottom performers</strong>: Remove bottom 20% from main ad groups</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Lock proven creatives</strong>: Set stable performers as regular placements</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Reserve new creatives</strong>: Update 20% of pool weekly to maintain freshness</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Document lessons learned</strong>: Record data and optimization actions as team asset</li>
</ul>
<h2>Quick FAQ</h2>
<p><strong>Q: Creatives are underperforming after 2 days—should I switch?</strong><br />
Check for these issues first: Does the hook grab attention in the first 3 seconds? Are selling points clearly conveyed? Is the audience targeting accurate? Resolve these before deciding to replace.</p>
<p><strong>Q: Are UGC-style creatives always better than professional shoots?</strong><br />
Not necessarily. While TikTok users prefer authenticity, overly rough content can damage brand trust. Aim for "professional script + authentic execution"—efficient messaging within platform aesthetics.</p>
<p><strong>Q: Should I chase trending topics during cold start?</strong><br />
适度参与平台热门话题是可以的，但需确保与产品有自然关联。生硬蹭热点的素材容易降低用户信任度，影响长期转化。</p>
<h2>Closing</h2>
<p>The core of TikTok Shop cold start is "testing for data." Creative pool building isn't about showcasing products—it's about giving your testing system enough "candidate answers." Following this checklist, most categories can identify efficient creative combinations within 2-4 weeks, keeping cold-start CAC within acceptable ranges.</p>
<p><strong>Next steps</strong>: Once creative testing stabilizes, shift focus to TikTok Shop live-streaming creatives and influencer collaboration content to further enrich your pool and improve overall conversion efficiency.</p>
